{"title":"Cambridge IGCSE Physics","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Cambridge IGCSE Physics","subtitle":"0625 - For examinations in 2026, 2027 and 2028","author":"Sugeng Riyanto, M.Sc.","date":"2026","format":{"html":{"toc":true,"number-sections":true,"theme":"cosmo"},"pdf":{"toc":true,"number-sections":true}}},"headingText":"Welcome to Cambridge IGCSE Physics","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\nThis textbook is designed to support students studying Cambridge IGCSE Physics (0625) for examinations in 2026, 2027, and 2028.\n\n### About This Book\n\nThis comprehensive resource covers all the topics in the Cambridge IGCSE Physics syllabus, including:\n\n- **Core Content**: Essential concepts all students must learn\n- **Supplement Content**: Extended material for students aiming for grades A* to C\n\n### Syllabus Overview\n\nThe syllabus is divided into six main topics:\n\n1. **Motion, Forces and Energy**\n2. **Thermal Physics**\n3. **Waves**\n4. **Electricity and Magnetism**\n5. **Nuclear Physics**\n6. **Space Physics**\n\n### Assessment Structure\n\n**Core Assessment** (Grades C-G):\n- Paper 1: Multiple Choice (45 minutes, 40 marks, 30%)\n- Paper 3: Theory (1 hour 15 minutes, 80 marks, 50%)\n- Paper 5 or 6: Practical (20%)\n\n**Extended Assessment** (Grades A*-G):\n- Paper 2: Multiple Choice (45 minutes, 40 marks, 30%)\n- Paper 4: Theory (1 hour 15 minutes, 80 marks, 50%)\n- Paper 5 or 6: Practical (20%)\n\n### How to Use This Book\n\n- Each chapter includes learning objectives aligned with the syllabus\n- Key concepts are highlighted for easy reference\n- Practice questions help reinforce understanding\n- Practical work sections develop experimental skills\n\n### Navigation\n\nUse the table of contents to navigate to specific chapters, or browse through the topics sequentially.\n\n---\n\n*This textbook is designed to complement classroom teaching and support independent study.*","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n## Welcome to Cambridge IGCSE Physics\n\nThis textbook is designed to support students studying Cambridge IGCSE Physics (0625) for examinations in 2026, 2027, and 2028.\n\n### About This Book\n\nThis comprehensive resource covers all the topics in the Cambridge IGCSE Physics syllabus, including:\n\n- **Core Content**: Essential concepts all students must learn\n- **Supplement Content**: Extended material for students aiming for grades A* to C\n\n### Syllabus Overview\n\nThe syllabus is divided into six main topics:\n\n1. **Motion, Forces and Energy**\n2. **Thermal Physics**\n3. **Waves**\n4. **Electricity and Magnetism**\n5. **Nuclear Physics**\n6. **Space Physics**\n\n### Assessment Structure\n\n**Core Assessment** (Grades C-G):\n- Paper 1: Multiple Choice (45 minutes, 40 marks, 30%)\n- Paper 3: Theory (1 hour 15 minutes, 80 marks, 50%)\n- Paper 5 or 6: Practical (20%)\n\n**Extended Assessment** (Grades A*-G):\n- Paper 2: Multiple Choice (45 minutes, 40 marks, 30%)\n- Paper 4: Theory (1 hour 15 minutes, 80 marks, 50%)\n- Paper 5 or 6: Practical (20%)\n\n### How to Use This Book\n\n- Each chapter includes learning objectives aligned with the syllabus\n- Key concepts are highlighted for easy reference\n- Practice questions help reinforce understanding\n- Practical work sections develop experimental skills\n\n### Navigation\n\nUse the table of contents to navigate to specific chapters, or browse through the topics sequentially.\n\n---\n\n*This textbook is designed to complement classroom teaching and support independent study.*"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":8,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"png","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":true,"freeze":false,"echo":false,"output":true,"warning":false,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"python":"C:/Users/